{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789804049,"nonce":"pPKqPndAmlKgXrkMxhWKKNckblo=","title":"Sets recomputed their small-int mask on every operation","message":"`zb_set_mask63` scanned every value of a set on each subset test,\ndifference and intersection: meteor-contest's `fp \u003c= free` scanned the\n50-position `free` set for every candidate footprint, a quarter of its\ntime. The mask is now cached in the table's first word (MASK_UNKNOWN\nuntil asked for, forgotten when a value is added; a set too small for a\ntable is scanned, it has at most eight values). The table grew by a word,\nwhich pushed the 64-slot table past the pool's 1 KB limit into libc, so\nthe pooled limit is now 2 KB. meteor-contest 44 ms to 41 ms.\n\nThe memory pressure test measures 400k steps against 5 MB: a program\nthat warms up compiles code and keeps the bodies later tiers recompile,\na step of about 4 MB that does not grow past it; the tiers are held still\nfor the runs (ZYNTAX_DISABLE_OSR).","files":null}]}